# Options for Presentation of Multilingual Text: Use of the Unicode Standard.

**Authors:** Erickson, Janet C., Sepehri, Abazar

## Abstract
Explains the development of standardized coding for digital text, especially for multilingual text, that has culminated in the Unicode standard. Topics include the University of Michigan's Humanities Text Initiative (HTI); a history of character sets; transliteration; non-Roman languages; fonts; and barriers to adoption of the Unicode standard. A glossary is appended. (54 references) (LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ557246

